có 70 contratos menores de servicios y suministros de más de 14.000 y hasta 15.000 euros, justo por debajo del límite legal. Si esos importes se repartieran como en la franja inmediatamente inferior, lo esperable serían 23,2 contratos. La razón entre observados y esperados es 3,0, con un intervalo de confianza del 95 % de 2,2 a 4,1. En diciembre se adjudicó el 3 % de los contratos junto al límite, mientras que diciembre supone el 7 % de todos sus contratos de servicios y suministros. Los contratos junto al límite se reparten entre 60 adjudicatarios distintos. El contrato [1], de 14.511 euros, se adjudicó en diciembre de 2025.\nQué no pueden demostrar: La concentración de contratos al límite no refleja actos ilícitos. Puede deberse a decisiones basadas en precios de mercado o necesidades específicas. No implica que se haya sobrepasado el límite ni que haya existido malversación.\nQué se puede revisar: Comprobar si los contratos [1], [2], [3] atienden necesidades similares. Verificar si en diciembre se contrataron otros servicios al límite. Analizar si los adjudicatarios repiten contratos en distintas fechas.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 70 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 23.2 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 3.0, with a 95% confidence interval of 2.2 to 4.1. December accounts for 3% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 7% of all its services and supplies contracts. The contracts just under the limit are spread across 60 different awardees. Contract [1], for 14,511 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The fact that many contracts are just under the legal limit does not prove any wrongdoing. It could reflect market pricing, budget constraints, or separate needs. Statistical patterns alone do not indicate improper actions by any party.\nWhat can be checked: Check the details of contract [1] to see what was purchased and the reason for the amount. Review the distribution of contracts across awardees to ensure no single provider was favored. Look at the dates to see if multiple contracts were awarded for similar needs in a short period.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["MF5BDYpmDi03vLk2DU2Ddg%3D%3D","alklgtSWNf6P%2Bo96UAV7cQ%3D%3D","cWtjnRcCmljN3k3tjedSGw%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-16"}}